---
// source: 6ba110cf70a7
import CaseLink from '../../components/CaseLink.astro';
import { severanceMonths, unfairAfter2012, unfairBefore2012 } from '../../content/examples';
import { euros, integer } from '../../content/format';
import type { Lang } from '../../i18n/languages';

interface Props {
  lang: Lang;
}
const { lang } = Astro.props;

const [months = 0] = severanceMonths(unfairAfter2012.calculation);
const [first = 0, second = 0] = severanceMonths(unfairBefore2012.calculation);
const decimal = (n: number) => String(n).replace('.', ',');
---

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="di-tramos">33 days per year, with a cap of 720</h3>
  <p>
    If the dismissal is acknowledged or declared unfair (improcedente), the severance pay is 33
    days’ pay per year worked, up to a maximum of 24 monthly payments, which is 720 days (art. 56.1
    ET). Time is counted in months, and part of a month counts as a whole month: 33 days a year is
    2,75 days per month.
  </p>
  <p>
    Your pay for each day is your annual pay, including the extra payments, divided by 365, as the
    CGPJ guide does. The calculator gives the figure to the cent and compares it with your
    employer’s.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>56</span> ET
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="di-2012">If you started before 12 February 2012</h3>
  <p>The severance pay is calculated in two periods (transitional provision 11.ª ET):</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Up to 11 February 2012, 45 days per year (3,75 per month).</li>
    <li>From 12 February 2012, 33 days per year (2,75 per month).</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    The total is capped at 720 days, unless the first period already goes beyond that. In that case
    only the first period counts, up to a maximum of 42 monthly payments (1.260 days).
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Transitional provision <span>11.ª</span> ET
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="di-ejemplo">Worked examples</h3>
  <p>
    A person earning 1.500&nbsp;€ gross a month with two extra payments of 1.500&nbsp;€,
    21.000&nbsp;€ a year. Their daily pay is 21.000&nbsp;€ / 365 ={' '}
    {euros(unfairAfter2012.dailySalary)}.
  </p>
  <p class="example">
    <span class="example__label">Contract from 2018</span> From 3 May 2018 to 20 July 2026,
    {integer(months)} months count. {integer(months)} × 2,75 = {decimal(unfairAfter2012.salaryDays)}{' '}
    days. 21.000&nbsp;€ × {decimal(unfairAfter2012.salaryDays)} / 365 ={' '}
    {euros(unfairAfter2012.amount)}.
  </p>
  <p class="example">
    <span class="example__label">Contract from 2010</span> From 1 March 2010 to 15 September 2026.
    First period: {integer(first)} months × 3,75 = {decimal(first * 3.75)} days. Second period:
    {integer(second)} months × 2,75 = {decimal(second * 2.75)} days. Total:{' '}
    {integer(unfairBefore2012.salaryDays)} days, below the cap. 21.000&nbsp;€ ×{' '}
    {integer(unfairBefore2012.salaryDays)} / 365 = {euros(unfairBefore2012.amount)}.
  </p>
  <p>
    The severance pay is separate from the final settlement (finiquito), which adds up the last
    month’s pay, untaken holiday and the accrued extra payments. The calculator reviews it all
    together.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="di-readmision">Reinstatement or severance pay</h3>
  <p>
    When a dismissal is declared unfair, the employer chooses within five days between reinstating
    you or paying you the severance pay (art. 56.1 ET). If it reinstates you, it also has to pay you
    back pay for the duration of proceedings (salarios de tramitación): the pay you did not receive
    from the dismissal onwards (art. 56.2 ET). If you are one of the workers’ legal representatives
    or a trade union delegate, the choice is yours (art. 56.4 ET).
  </p>
  <p>
    This review does not calculate back pay for the duration of proceedings, nor does it decide
    whether a dismissal is unfair: that is declared by a court or acknowledged by the employer.
  </p>
  <p class="folio">
    Art. <span>56</span> ET
  </p>
</section>

<section class="sheet sheet--text">
  <h3 id="di-otros">Other dismissals</h3>
  <p>
    An objective-grounds dismissal is paid at 20 days per year, with 15 days’ notice: you will find
    it in <CaseLink lang={lang} id="objective_dismissal" />. Any dismissal, including a disciplinary
    one, is a legal situation of unemployment: <CaseLink lang={lang} id="benefit_disciplinary" />{' '}
    explains which ways of leaving a job give you unemployment benefit.
  </p>
</section>
